# ============================================================
# THE IMPORTANT LINE IS THE FIRST ONE. READ THE COMMENT.
# ============================================================
#
# _source/ holds the raw resume and portfolio extracts, the content plan
# (including its unresolved "GAPS — ANDREW MUST SUPPLY" section), the SEO
# plan and the deployment research. It is working material. It is not for
# publication.
#
# This site ships a .nojekyll file, which disables Jekyll on GitHub Pages.
# Jekyll is the thing that normally hides folders whose names start with an
# underscore. With .nojekyll present, anything committed under _source/ would
# be served publicly at https://your-domain/_source/resume.txt and read by
# anyone with the URL.
#
# So: _source/ never enters the repository. robots.txt also disallows it as a
# second layer, but Disallow only asks crawlers politely — it does not stop
# access. Keeping the folder out of git is the actual protection.
#
# If you ever need those files on another machine, copy them across directly
# or keep them in a separate PRIVATE repository. Do not remove the line below.

_source/


# --- macOS / Windows / editor junk -----------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Anything you are drafting but have not decided to publish --------------
*.draft.html
*.draft.md
/drafts/
/notes/
/scratch/

# --- Superseded stylesheets ------------------------------------------------
# GitHub Pages serves every file in the repo as a public URL; it has no idea
# which ones the pages actually link to. An old stylesheet left in assets/css/
# is 56KB of dead weight anyone can download. Keep old versions outside the
# repo — ../_archive/site-css/ is where the Broadsheet one went.
*-backup.css
*.old.css

# --- Never commit secrets ---------------------------------------------------
# The site has no build step and no server, so there should be nothing here.
# These exist so that a stray file from a tutorial or a form-backend key never
# lands in a public repo by accident.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets.*

# --- Tooling state that must never ship -------------------------------------
.omc/
.claude/
